ONNX Runtime (pinned ORT_VERSION): fix MultiHeadAttention's ROCm "Generic"
(non-Composable-Kernel) fallback pipeline to transpose Q/K/V into the layout
its own GEMMs require, instead of refusing to run whenever query
sequence_length > 1.

WHY
---
onnxruntime/contrib_ops/rocm/bert/batched_gemm_softmax_gemm_permute_pipelines.cuh
implements the Q*K'->softmax->*V computation behind MultiHeadAttention two
ways: a Composable Kernel (CK) path, and a "Generic" fallback built from plain
rocBLAS GEMMs plus a custom softmax kernel. This image builds ORT with
`onnxruntime_USE_COMPOSABLE_KERNEL=OFF` (gfx803 has no matrix-core hardware
for CK to target), so Generic is the *only* path available here.

Generic's own doc comment at the top of the file says its GEMMs expect Q, K, V
already permuted to BNSH ("In QKV projection (prior to this pipeline): Q
[B,S,N*H] ->Reshape-> [B,S,N,H] ->Permute0213-> [B,N,S,H]"). That permute
happens upstream, inside a fused QKV-projection kernel -- but MultiHeadAttention
called with three separate, raw Q/K/V tensors (mode BSNH_BLNH_BLNH_NONE_NONE_
NONE_NONE in this file's own mode table, documented there as "MHA basic", the
single most ordinary self/cross-attention call shape) has no such projection
step. Nothing ever transposes Q, K, V for that mode. GetSupportedStatus()
knows this and rejects it outright:

    case BSNH_BLNH_BLNH_NONE_NONE_NONE_NONE:
      return TUNABLE_OP_UNSUPPORTED("GenericPipeline only supports qkv_format
      as Q_K_V_BNSH but k, v are BLNH");

-- with one exception: when sequence_length == 1, a [1,H] slice per head is
byte-identical whether you call it BSNH or BNSH, so the check is skipped.
Real multi-token attention has no such luck, and since CK is compiled out on
this image, there is no other registered op left to try. The observable
symptom, from onnxruntime_test_all:

    Could not find viable op

for MultiHeadAttentionTest.CrossAttention_Batch1_HeadSize8 (batch=1,
num_heads=2, head_size=8, sequence_length=2, kv_sequence_length=3 -- an
entirely ordinary shape). head_size=8 is incidental (it's just ROCm MHA's
documented minimum head_size); the real trigger is query sequence_length > 1
under this mode, which any real cross- or self-attention call with more than
one query token will hit.

This is not a rocBLAS or MIOpen bug: rocBLAS is never even called for this
case -- the rejection happens in ORT's own C++ dispatch, one layer above any
GPU kernel invocation. That's why the fix lives here rather than in a
rocBLAS/MIOpen patch.

Confirmed via isolating the exact failing test and reading the real error
(not just "verifier shows no mismatch" -- there was no GEMM call to verify):
`rocblasGemmBatchedHelper`/`TunableOp::FindFastestImpl` both fail identically
because GetSupportedStatus rejects the call before any kernel launches.

WHAT
----
ORT already has a utility for exactly this transpose, `LaunchTransQkv`
(onnxruntime/contrib_ops/rocm/bert/attention_impl.h), used elsewhere for the
plain fused `Attention` op's own QKV-projection permute. With `matrix_num=1`
it degenerates to a plain BSNH -> BNSH copy per tensor, which is exactly what's
missing here. Added:

- `GetQkvTransposeExtraBytes` / extended `GetWorkspaceNumBytes`: reserve extra
  workspace for three transposed (BNSH) copies of Q, K, V, appended after the
  existing gemm1_out/softmax_out/gemm2_out region so it can never alias it.
- `TransposeQkvForBasicMha`: runs the three `LaunchTransQkv` calls (V uses
  `v_head_size`, not `head_size` -- they can differ) and returns a shallow
  copy of the params struct pointing at the transposed buffers.
  `GemmSoftmaxGemmPermuteParams` owns no resources, so the copy is safe.
- `Run()`: for this one mode, transpose first and use the transposed params
  for the rest of the pipeline; every other mode is untouched.
- `GetSupportedStatus()`: the case now returns `Status::OK()` instead of
  rejecting -- Run() handles the transpose it used to be missing.

Verified: MultiHeadAttentionTest.CrossAttention_Batch1_HeadSize8 passes (fp16
output matches the CPU reference). Full MultiHeadAttentionTest/AttentionTest/
DecoderAttentionTest families: 53 passed, 0 failed, 13 pre-existing explicit
ROCM_GTEST_SKIP skips, no regressions. onnxruntime_test_all: 12 -> 3 failures.

Applies to: ORT's ROCm EP with USE_COMPOSABLE_KERNEL=OFF -- not gfx803-specific
in principle (any ROCm target building without CK hits the same gap), but only
verified on gfx803 here. See mha-basic-mode-no-viable-op.sh for how this patch
is applied and verified at build time.

--- a/onnxruntime/contrib_ops/rocm/bert/batched_gemm_softmax_gemm_permute_pipelines.cuh
+++ b/onnxruntime/contrib_ops/rocm/bert/batched_gemm_softmax_gemm_permute_pipelines.cuh
